  "id": "self-conscious-emotion",
  "term": "self-conscious emotion",
  "definition": "A self-conscious emotion is an emotion such as embarrassment, shame, or pride that involves the self and has a distinct nonverbal expression. Research described in the packet treats these emotions as a group whose expressions can be recognized, although recognition varies across cultures.",
